<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04T6">Remark <span data-tag="04T6">10.1.5.3</span>.</a> In the augmented simplex category $\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{+}$, there is a unique morphism $\delta ^{0}_{0}: [-1] \rightarrow [0]$. This morphism determines a fully faithful functor $[1] \rightarrow \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{+}$, whose image is the full subcategory $\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{+}^{\leq 0} \subseteq \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{+}$ spanned by the objects $[0]$ and $[-1]$. Combining Remarks <a data-tag="04SX" href="/tag/04SX">10.1.4.2</a> and <a data-tag="04K2" href="/tag/04K2">7.3.2.4</a>, we see that an augmented simplicial object $X_{\bullet }$ of an $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is a Čech nerve if and only if it is right Kan extended from the subcategory $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{+}^{\leq 0} )^{\operatorname{op}} \subset \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{+} )^{\operatorname{op}}$. </p>
